  "id": "Compound::DB00619 - Gene::771",
  "verbalization": "Imatinib is likely to interact with Ca12 through a series of molecular mechanisms involving the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide. The evidence suggests that Imatinib binds to Ca7, which then participates in the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide, an activity that is also exhibited by Ca12. This implies a potential functional link between Imatinib and Ca12, where the binding of Imatinib to Ca7 may influence the activity of Ca12 in this biochemical process. Similarly, Imatinib's interaction with Ca7 could also affect the carbonate dehydratase activity of Ca7, which in turn is linked to Ca12. These findings suggest that Imatinib may modulate the activity of Ca12 through a pathway involving the reversible hydration of carbon dioxide, potentially by altering the functional state of Ca7. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Imatinib influences Ca12, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
